# The application icons of candy-icons that build_files/base/10-icons.sh leaves in the theme, one
# name a line, without the .svg. Every other drawing in the pack's apps/scalable is deleted, and the
# names that linked to it with it, so that application shows the icon its maker gave it.
#
# The pack draws most applications as their maker's logo in its own gradients. A logo is a
# trademark, and its owner decides how it looks: Mozilla, JetBrains, Anthropic and the rest allow
# theirs unaltered or not at all. So a name belongs here only if its drawing is one of these:
#
#   - a pictogram of a job (a calculator, a folder, an envelope), not of a product. Some are filed
#     under the name of the KDE or GNOME tool the pack drew them for; what matters is the drawing.
#   - the logo of an application this image ships whose maker claims no trademark in it and
#     publishes no terms for it. Check the maker's repository and site before adding one.
#
# The name does not settle it: utilities-tweak-tool is a specification name, and the pack draws it
# as the Nintendo Switch logo, so it is not here.
#
# A name upstream adds later is left out until somebody has looked at the drawing and put it here.
# `20-tests.sh` fails if the theme carries an application icon that is neither here nor drawn for
# this image.

